==Strategy==
==='''Chapter 1'''===
You have a lot of time to save up early on. A single Zoge heads your way after you reach Worker Cat level 4, then a single Zackie Peng and a Zang Roo come out about 15 seconds later. Send out Cats when you see the first Zoge so that you can force them to burrow before they get to your base. Once you down the Zang and Zackie, a couple more Zoge spawn as your Cats head to the enemy base.

Once the base reaches 99% the rest of the enemies spawn and the peons begin to spawn again. A Cadaver Bear and Dread Bore burrow immediately and will be probably well past your initial wave of damage dealers when they resurface. A well timed Cat Cannon or Holyblast can keep them from burrowing and allows your front line DPS to be protected. Keeping an Uber in reserve to deal with them incase the Cannon tactic fails is a good idea, the pair of them can work their way through your meatshields awful quick, if you're not careful.

Lord Gravey has 100% knockback chance and high damage per hit. Your meatshields will be damaged a lot so bringing meatshields with survive ability like [[Pogo Cat (Rare Cat)|Jiangshi Cat]] or Cameraman Cat is a good idea (Cameraman also has great DPS to help out with the backline). With the mediocre range on Gravey it's only a matter of time until your heavy hitting Zombie Killers take him out. If you can manage the Dread Bore/Bear combo then Gravey is a cake walk.

==='''Chapter 2'''===
Before attacking the base and triggering the wave of the main threats, you should save up your money. Thankfully, the stage sends out 3 Mistress Celeboodles at the very beginning of the stage, making that task a lot easier.

Once the base is triggered, that's when the real challenge begins. Due to the presence of Miss Haka, you should bring a Holy Blast cannon along if you fail to inflict enough DPS against her to keep knocking her back before she can burrow. As for the I.M Phace and Elizabeth, some anti-alien Crowd Control units should be enough to subdue and kill them.

